      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There isn't a single \"right\" way, as schools rarely choose only one approach; instead, the trend is to build the foundation on shared values and social cohesion before introducing critical analysis to deepen understanding. Teaching students to question systemic issues is crucial for democracy, but it builds best upon a baseline of pride and unity that makes civic engagement feel constructive rather than antagonistic. Ultimately, the most effective path integrates unity as the goal with inquiry as the method, ensuring both respect and critical thinking develop in tandem.",
